		{
			"ID": "20260927112821-dmce6cp",
			"Type": "NodeHeading",
			"HeadingLevel": 3,
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20260927112821-dmce6cp",
				"updated": "20261012014930"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Conditional colors"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20260927112821-u18f0d0",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20260927112821-u18f0d0",
				"updated": "20260927112821"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Open the database view settings and choose "
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeTextMark",
					"TextMarkType": "kbd",
					"TextMarkTextContent": "Conditional colors"
				},
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " to add a rule. Select one field and a condition, then choose a background color and its target. Changes take effect immediately and support undo and redo."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20260927112821-xoxibjc",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20260927112821-xoxibjc",
				"updated": "20260927112821"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Rules belong to the current view. Table, list, calendar, kanban, and gallery views support entry backgrounds. Table views also support coloring the property used by the condition. Property rules remain stored but do not apply in other layouts."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20260927112821-7hfkus2",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20260927112821-7hfkus2",
				"updated": "20260927123058"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Each rule evaluates its own single-field condition; rules are not combined with AND. Drag a rule by its handle to change priority, including on touch screens. The first matching rule for each property wins. A matching entry rule colors the remaining area and stops evaluation; earlier property colors are retained. Default background also counts as a match."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20260927112821-qw0iuyn",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20260927112821-qw0iuyn",
				"updated": "20260927112821"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "For example, place a blue property rule first and a green entry rule second. An entry matching both keeps that property blue and uses green elsewhere. Move the green entry rule first to make the whole entry green."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20260927112821-e6uldts",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20260927112821-e6uldts",
				"updated": "20260927112821"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "For select and multi-select fields, Match first option uses the first selected option in the entry, including its default color; it does not use the order of option definitions. You can also choose a fixed built-in or custom color. Conditions use the existing filter operators and can use rendered values when available."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20260927112821-ks3ham9",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20260927112821-ks3ham9",
				"updated": "20260927112821"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Colors do not change field values or filter out entries. Hidden fields can still drive rules. Incomplete conditions and rules referring to deleted fields do not apply. Copying a view copies its rules; editing one view does not change the other. Existing calendar option colors remain available as a compatible rule, and deleting all rules clears the colors."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20260613171129-edm1pru",
			"Type": "NodeHeading",
			"HeadingLevel": 2,
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20260613171129-edm1pru",
				"updated": "20261024163429"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Filtering, sorting, and grouping"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20260613171129-n8nqdp1",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20260613171129-n8nqdp1",
				"updated": "20260613171129"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Each view can independently configure filter conditions and sort rules; filters and sorts do not affect each other across views."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20260613171129-5zjv62o",
			"Type": "NodeHeading",
