				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": " from the database block toolbar and select a configured Relation field, or a Rollup targeting a Relation field with Show original values or Show unique values. The panel lists all eligible fields in the database, but only one can be enabled at a time. Select another field to switch to it; select the checked field again to turn off the context filter. "
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261012014737-oo845s9",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261012014737-oo845s9",
				"updated": "20261012014859"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "Once enabled, the fixed condition “Contains any item - Current document” applies to every view in this database block. Each view’s ordinary filters remain independent and are combined with the context filter using AND. "
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"ID": "20261012014737-507hutv",
			"Type": "NodeParagraph",
			"Properties": {
				"id": "20261012014737-507hutv",
				"updated": "20261012014859"
			},
			"Children": [
				{
					"Type": "NodeText",
					"Data": "The current document must already be bound to an item in the final related database; otherwise, no matching items are shown and you cannot add items from this database block. With a direct Relation field, new items automatically relate to the current document. With a Rollup, new items do not fill the computed value or change relations in the intermediate database, and may be hidden by the filter. "
				}
			]
		},
